# Keep shell scripts LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the common Windows default) rewrites checked-out files
# to CRLF. For a script this is fatal when it is COPYed into an image: the
# shebang becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, the kernel looks for an interpreter named
# "/bin/sh\r", and the container dies with
#   exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# even though the file is plainly there. Force LF so the image built from a
# Windows checkout matches the image built from CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
